{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"openclaw-office-toolkit","displayName":"Office Toolkit","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/axelhu/skills/openclaw-office-toolkit","publisherHandle":"axelhu","publisherDisplayName":"AxelHu","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/axelhu","version":"1.0.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1775039294136,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/openclaw-office-toolkit/card?ownerHandle=axelhu&version=1.0.0","sha256":"aedaefeed2af107047e7ed0fbbe4bd1dc75771d7b374397f606613280ee8bacf","size":1832,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"7864ab7dffbac2bbbea41b8cbb4946e0868850e7fe7ea0e1e9b9f3e817109bf4","bundleFingerprints":["3c9e7d370f9230a64e03a90eab464a50632c2c50c36044679eb7e53a06de1980","2795596176a7d1b16366926654032a3496f93561faf8f2de800452aa2c3024d1"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":5512,"sha256":"572d8733350b59ce8a19cb5a2e51db9ca747a486f08423aaa1204598614fc765","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"_meta.json","size":430,"sha256":"22cc245d215f81a34e9d022f716e31018596d5807433d72012942ef3d6729e01","contentType":"application/json"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a coherent Office document helper, but its setup instructions ask users to modify the host system with privileged, unpinned installs.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789532865196,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T08","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unpinned System-Wide Dependency Installation"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":13,"endLine":14}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"c961cff1b63033d7"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n\n  **File Location**: `SKILL.md`, lines 13–14  \n  **Vulnerability Type**: Unpinned dependencies and unsafe system-wide package installation  \n  **Risk Level**: Medium\n\n  **Complete Code Snippet**:\n\n  ```bash\n  pip install --break-system-packages python-docx openpyxl python-pptx pypdf\n  sudo apt install libreoffice-writer libreoffice-calc libreoffice-impress pandoc\n  ```\n\n  ### Technical Analysis\n\n  The installation instructions do not pin Python or operating-system package versions and do not verify package hashes. Consequently, the installed code depends on mutable upstream package repositories rather than a reviewed, reproducible dependency set.\n\n  The `--break-system-packages` option explicitly bypasses Python's externally managed environment protection and permits modification of the host's system Python environment. This can overwrite or conflict with packages used by other applications. The `sudo apt install` command additionally performs privileged host-level changes, although no malicious package source or deliberate privilege-escalation mechanism was found in the audited files.\n\n  Exploitation depends on a dependency source being compromised, a malicious release being published under a resolved package name, or an unexpected upstream version introducing harmful installation or runtime behavior.\n\n  ### Attack Path\n\n  1. An Agent or user follows the environment setup instructions.\n  2. `pip` resolves the latest available releases because no versions or hashes are specified.\n  3. A compromised or unexpectedly changed package is downloaded from the configured package index.\n  4. Package installation logic executes and modifies the system Python environment because `--break-system-packages` is enabled.\n  5. Malicious or vulnerable dependency code may subsequently execute when the document-processing libraries are imported or used.\n  6. Separately, the `sudo apt install` instruction installs host-level packages with administrative privileges from the configured OS repositories.\n\n  ### Impact Assessment\n\n  A malicious Python dependency could execute code with the privileges of the account running `pip`. If the command is run by an administrator, its effective scope may extend to system-level modification. Even without a malicious dependency, system-wide installation can cause dependency conflicts, overwrite shared packages, destabilize unrelated applications, and reduce environment reproducibility.\n\n  The privileged OS-package command can modify the host installation, but the audited project does not provide evidence of a malicious repository, package substitution, persistence mechanism, credential theft, or intentional privilege escalation.","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n  1. Create and use a dedicated virtual environment rather than modifying the system Python installation.\n  2. Remove `--break-system-packages` from the installation command.\n  3. Pin every Python dependency to a reviewed version in a requirements or lock file.\n  4. Use hash verification, such as `pip install --require-hashes -r requirements.txt`, with reviewed hashes.\n  5. Perform dependency vulnerability and provenance checks before publication and on every update.\n  6. Require explicit user approval before installing operating-system packages with `sudo`.\n  7. Pin OS package versions where operationally practical and use only trusted, authenticated repositories.\n  8. Update `_meta.json` to declare the required binaries accurately, because it currently reports an empty `anyBinaries` list despite the documented reliance on Pandoc and LibreOffice."}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":75,"primaryLanguage":"JSON","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789532804.9332912,"endTime":1789532836.3379192}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"office-toolkit","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v5764c9ehfkeg5fbmsmwywk7en8eh9bx-btG5cH/clawscan-skillspector-203505109/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-16T04:26:43.898314+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":47,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"MEDIUM"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":228,"executable":false,"size_bytes":5512,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"_meta.json","type":"json","lines":18,"executable":false,"size_bytes":430,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-ab92c72b71514e68b9739834824472ba","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":13,"end_line":16},"finding":null,"explanation":"The installation instructions include privileged package installation and `--break-system-packages` without warning about system integrity or least-privilege concerns. This can encourage unsafe environment modification and increase the blast radius if users follow the instructions blindly.","remediation":"Remove `--break-system-packages` unless absolutely necessary, prefer virtual environments, add clear warnings about privileged installation, and separate optional system dependencies from core Python package setup.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":13,"end_line":16}]},{"id":"PE2","finding_id":"finding-7a4641cf59a34eb88f2920b158fee9c6","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Sudo/Root Execution","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":15,"end_line":null},"finding":"sudo ","explanation":"The documented use of `sudo apt install` normalizes root-level execution in a skill, which is risky in agent ecosystems because users may execute setup steps without understanding the trust implications. Elevated installation increases the consequences of mistakes, compromised package sources, or copy-pasted modifications.","remediation":"Prefer non-root installation paths where possible, document that root privileges are only for optional system packages, recommend reviewing commands before execution, and provide safer alternatives such as containerized setup or prebuilt environments.","code_snippet":"\n```bash\npip install --break-system-packages python-docx openpyxl python-pptx pypdf\nsudo apt install libreoffice-writer libreoffice-calc libreoffice-impress pandoc\n```\n\n## 快速参考","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","contextual-triage","likely-benign-context"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"16746f7044f347c6322d4c5b879b3fb06b2f205cbf1c9a209b43d52b34b3afd7","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":15,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-5fe8d573d78b432093e83ff132c35ad0","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":44,"end_line":46},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill invokes an external binary (`pandoc`) through `subprocess.run`, which increases capability beyond pure in-process library use and can become dangerous if later adapted to accept untrusted arguments or file paths without validation. External tool execution also broadens the attack surface and may process malformed documents with vulnerabilities in the converter.","remediation":"Prefer in-process libraries where possible. If `pandoc` is required, strictly use fixed argument lists, validate and constrain input paths, avoid shell invocation, document the external execution behavior, and consider sandboxing/confining the converter process.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":44,"end_line":46}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-c87793f85f18412db912310faff00ee7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":50,"end_line":75},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill provides direct file creation and modification examples without emphasizing overwrite risk, backup practices, or safe output-path handling. In an agent context, this can lead to unintended destruction or replacement of user files when operating on sensitive documents.","remediation":"Add explicit warnings before write operations, require confirmation before overwriting existing files, default to new output filenames, and recommend backups or temporary-output workflows before replacing originals.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":50,"end_line":75}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-64c0e596af4843c9bb9116aeb0800078","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":79,"end_line":79},"finding":null,"explanation":"While Office document editing is in scope, the recommendation at L079 relies on launching LibreOffice rather than the documented Python libraries. Invoking a desktop application is a materially broader operational capability and is not clearly disclosed in the manifest description beyond a brief dependency mention.","remediation":"Clarify in the manifest that the skill may invoke external desktop tools like LibreOffice for editing/validation, or remove that guidance if the skill should remain library-only.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":79,"end_line":79}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-459197763aa54cce8f80b672e7a2dd8b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":24,"end_line":24},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest at L003 says the skill is based on python-docx, openpyxl, python-pptx, and pypdf. The quick reference at L024 states Excel reading may use pandas, which introduces behavior and dependency outside the described implementation scope.","remediation":"Either remove pandas from the documented implementation options or update the manifest to declare pandas as part of the skill's supported toolchain/dependencies.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":24,"end_line":24}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-0fdf83da573b467591ff344c72d8fe15","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":30,"end_line":30},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest description at L003 limits the skill to reading, creating, and editing Office/PDF documents using python-docx, openpyxl, python-pptx, and pypdf. The quick reference at L030 adds a separate image-conversion capability using pdftoppm, which goes beyond the stated document-handling scope and is not disclosed in the manifest description.","remediation":"Either remove the PDF-to-image conversion guidance, or update the manifest description to explicitly include document rendering/image conversion and the required poppler-utils dependency.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":30,"end_line":30}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-71fce60f191e4468a30a3cefcc2901e6","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"_meta.json","start_line":12,"end_line":12},"finding":null,"explanation":"The credential setup description is written as Chinese-only text (\"无凭证需求。\") in a manifest that otherwise provides no indication that the skill is region- or language-specific. This can violate language/locale policy because it forces a specific language without documented user opt-in or justification.","remediation":"Provide the description in a default/shared language for the skill ecosystem, or include multilingual text and document any intended locale scope or user language selection behavior.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"_meta.json","start_line":12,"end_line":12}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":false,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1584,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1598},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":3746,"completion_tokens":624,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":4370},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1575,"completion_tokens":154,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1729},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":3737,"completion_tokens":300,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":4037},{"node":"semantic_security_discovery","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":3269,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":3283},{"node":"semantic_security_